    {
      "id": "43788650",
      "title": "Transforming Template Data with Pipes",
      "lectureOrder": 58,
      "videoOrder": 54,
      "sourceHash": "ace582a6c5f96b0ad67dd4ada0300f9aec6db71c0ef4190adf8a5c66aafd3a3d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.91,
          "en": "Another pretty important feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.91,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "offered by Angular is the feature of pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "which in the end are output transformers you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "things that transform output in templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 17.82,
          "en": "And a good example for such a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.82,
          "end": 21.48,
          "en": "can be seen in the task.component.html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.48,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "Because here, we of course have this date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 27.39,
          "en": "this due date, which we're outputting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.39,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "At the moment, it looks like this, which is not horrible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 35.073,
          "en": "but maybe also not the most human readable way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "To output this in a nicer way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 43.34,
          "en": "we can funnel this value through a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "by using this pipe symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 50.43,
          "en": "this vertical bar here after task.dueDate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.43,
          "end": 53.16,
          "en": "And then after this pipe symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.16,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "we add one of the pipes defined by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "so one of the pipes built into Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "And you can also build your own pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "and we'll do that later in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 67.02,
          "en": "but for now, we'll use a built-in one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.02,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "And the built-in pipe I wanna use is the date pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "which as the name suggests is a transformer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "that's provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 81.68,
          "en": "that aims to format dates in a more human readable way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "Now, this date pipe currently is unknown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "and at least at the point of time where I'm recording this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "I also don't get such a import suggestion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "But that's, of course, no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "We can import it manually in the task component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 103.03999999999999,
          "en": "by importing the DatePipe written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.572,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "from @angular/common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "So not from core, but from common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.31,
          "end": 114.15,
          "en": "And then we add the DatePipe next to the CardComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.15,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "here in the imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 118.32,
          "en": "With that, it's unlocked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 121.14,
          "en": "and it will now transform this date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 122.943,
          "en": "As you can see, if you saved this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.86,
          "end": 128.7,
          "en": "now this is formatted in a more human readable way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.7,
          "end": 132.39,
          "en": "Now, this DatePipe also can be configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 136.5,
          "en": "so that you can control how the date should be formatted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 140.43,
          "en": "and you find more information in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.43,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "There, you also find a more detailed description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "and also detailed usage notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 150,
          "en": "Because in the end, those Angular pipes can be configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150,
          "end": 152.5,
          "en": "by adding a colon after the pipe name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "and then thereafter any parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 159.153,
          "en": "any configuration that should be passed to the pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.68,
          "en": "For example, here, we could pass the string short",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.68,
          "end": 168.68,
          "en": "to the DatePipe so that we get this formatting style here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "So if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 173.883,
          "en": "we now would have this short formatting look here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "Now, in my case, that's actually not what I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 180.87,
          "en": "Instead, I want this full date formatting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 185.87,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll use fullDate as an option here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 189.03,
          "en": "And with that, I get this output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.03,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "which in my opinion looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 194.133,
          "en": "And that's the concept of working with pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
